/T (THE MISSION: ENDPOINT HARDENING What is Endpoint Hardening? : It is the process of securing a computer system by reducing its Attack Surface. This involves removing unnecessary software, disabling unused services, and most importantly enforcing the Principle of Least Privilege \(PoLP\).)
/E (THE MISSION: ENDPOINT HARDENING What is Endpoint Hardening? : It is the process of securing a computer system by reducing its Attack Surface. This involves removing unnecessary software, disabling unused services, and most importantly enforcing the Principle of Least Privilege \(PoLP\).)
